+    // register locals, so alias them instead of copying (pfStageIfAliases pays the copy only if one
+    // of those registers is written before the flags are consumed -- in a compare-and-branch, never).
+    // ...but only when the very next instruction is the conditional branch that consumes them. Then
+    // nothing can write the aliased registers in between, which is what makes the alias safe without
+    // any further analysis. (A wider window needs the write tracking to be airtight everywhere a
